# Read by aquasecurity/trivy-action in the `images` CI job (.github/workflows/ci.yml).
#
# All entries below are Go-stdlib CVEs inside the Caddy binary bundled in the
# upstream `caddy:alpine` base image (frontend/Dockerfile, landing/Dockerfile,
# admin/Dockerfile). Trivy reports them as "fixed" because a fix exists in Go
# itself, but caddy:alpine hasn't been rebuilt against a patched Go toolchain
# yet. There is nothing to change on our side until upstream rebuilds; remove
# entries here as each stops appearing in a scan (meaning caddy:alpine has
# caught up).
#
# 2026-10-09: caddy:alpine is Caddy v2.11.7 built with go1.26.8 (pushed
# 2026-10-06). The fix is in Go 1.26.9 / 1.27.2, released 2026-10-08. The 16
# entries from 2026-09-18 (Caddy v2.11.4) no longer appear and were removed.
# 2026-10-10: one more, CVE-2026-78669 (HIGH): net/http2 denial of service through
# excessive HTTP/2 SETTINGS frames. Trivy lists it twice for the same Caddy binary:
# golang.org/x/net v0.59.0 (fixed in 0.60.0) and Go stdlib 1.26.8 (fixed in 1.26.9 / 1.27.2).
# caddy:alpine is still the 2026-10-06 build (Caddy v2.11.7, go1.26.8), so the fix is not
# available to us yet. Remove this entry when a scan stops reporting it.
CVE-2026-78667
CVE-2026-97031
CVE-2026-78669
